<title>SPAIN: BBV lowers preferential rate by 50 bp.</title>
<headline>BBV lowers preferential rate by 50 bp.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Bilbao Vizcaya on Wednesday announced it was lowering its preferential rate by a half-point to nine percent from 9.5 percent.</p>
<p>It also lowered its variable mortgage rate by 50 basis points to 7.50 percent while the consumer credit rate fell a quarter-point to 13.25 percent.</p>
<p>BBV is the last of the large Spanish banks to lower rates after the Bank of Spain cut its key money market rate by a half-point to 6.75 percent on Thursday.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
